<title>SWITZERLAND: Unilabs 1996/97 sales rise 10 pct.</title>
<headline>Unilabs 1996/97 sales rise 10 pct.</headline>
<dateline>GENEVA 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Unilabs SA, a Geneva-based clinical laboratory group, said sales in the 1996/97 financial year, which ended May 31, rose 10 percent to 127 million Swiss francs, in line with the forecast issued in connection with its initial public offering in April.</p>
<p>Unilabs also said in a statement its management expected a considerable rise in 1996/97 cash-flow and operating earnings.</p>
<p>&quot;In light of the good result, the board of directors will propose the payout of a dividend at the next shareholders' meeting,&quot; Unilabs also said.</p>
<p>It added that detailed results would be published later, but it did not say when.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
